  "body": "## Problem and observed result\n\nThis adds a reproducible compatibility trial for Anthropic's Competitive Brief Skill, comparing three original-Skill runs with a genuinely generated LazyMind Workflow on a fixed Linear-versus-Asana PM task.\n\n**Draft deliberately:** automatic installation, Preflight, model-backed conversion and publication succeeded, but the autonomous external task failed after 2/5 steps. An official step-scoped retry and two subsequent advances completed the same unchanged Workflow session. The original external task remains failed. The recovered report has groundedness issues, both tested artifact-edit routes failed, and human review is pending. This is not submitted as a successful autonomous Showcase.\n\n## Skill and test environment\n\n- Source: anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins, `marketing/skills/competitive-brief/SKILL.md`, commit `c75fda00ff0e41c8ee331ae312c8a07f1967653b`.\n- Original Skill Git blob: `1a7df218996ed350c67e6899a60321f205bb69d6`. Source/license links and the missing parent CONNECTORS reference are documented; no upstream Skill body is redistributed.\n- macOS arm64; Codex CLI 0.155.0-alpha.9 baseline; local LazyMind connection reported DeepSeek `deepseek-flash`.\n- Audited/tested main: `71a0e5a829f1ef8d9a5d9e9ce720386ba3c69d0e`. The deployed Core has a recorded SHA-256 but no VCS revision, so deployed E2E and current-main regression evidence are kept separate.\n- Same frozen business task and seven paraphrased official-source cards, collected live on 2026-10-27. Both execution modes used explicitly labelled **offline replay**. No paid database or private business material.\n\n## Conversion and execution\n\n- The supplied-style `/blob/.../SKILL.md` link failed installation. A pinned `/tree/.../competitive-brief` URL worked through `POST /external-agent/workflow-tasks`.\n- Published Workflow: `competitive_brief`, revision `617f74c8-30fc-42da-84a6-0893f8fda218`; five genuinely generated steps.\n- Analysis attempt 1 wrote intermediate JSON but was rejected for missing the downstream final Markdown brief. The exact failure, scoped retry, successful attempt and unchanged generated package are preserved.\n- Original-Skill reports: 3/3 delivered; 146.286 / 212.477 / 133.378 seconds.\n- Autonomous hosted task: failed after 615.843 seconds; 28 observed execution-step tool calls. Assisted session completion added 3 tool calls. No invocation-count or dollar-cost claims.\n- All four reports have the seven sections and correct four paid-plan annual seat subtotals. The recovered report does not fully pass groundedness acceptance; concrete overclaims are listed.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\n`examples/competitive-brief-skill2workflow/` contains bilingual READMEs, REPRODUCTION.md, EVALUATION.md, SOURCES.md, implementation audit and an independent issue record.\n\n`evidence/` includes 74 hashed files: fixed inputs, acquisition hashes, three baseline reports/events/usage records, actual generated package, sanitized HTTP and tool-event records, artifact revisions, failures/recovery requests, real Panel screenshots and regression logs. Account identifiers, private paths, credentials, upstream source bodies and internal reasoning are excluded.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Evidence verifier: 74 hashes, four report structure/arithmetic checks, 16 Markdown files, 82 local links; recorded failure outcomes asserted.\n- Python syntax and reproduction CLI smoke check.\n- Current-main Go source-URL and focused hosted conversion/task tests passed.\n- Current-main Python Workflow SDK / agent-kit tests: **92 passed**.\n\n## Limits and distinction from existing examples\n\nNo production Core/Runtime changes, no manually substituted Workflow, no synthetic screenshot or claimed human approval. Generated nodes have no mandatory review gate; the deployed Panel reports inherited full-trust execution. Artifact PATCH returned 503 and native slot PATCH returned 500; the report stayed unchanged.\n\nThis is not the built-in manually adapted Product Solution Delivery package and does not reuse it as conversion proof. Unlike #852's Superpowers dispatch/native Brief experiment, this records a pinned external knowledge-work Skill, real hosted automatic conversion, matched-source baseline runs and an actual intermediate/final acceptance mismatch. The example indexes label it a compatibility trial.\n\nNot established: autonomous E2E success, repeated conversion stability, successful human editing/approval, same-model performance, live retrieval quality, exact deployed commit or cost savings.",
